+## Evidence
+
+### skills/fetch-helper — autonomous
+
+- `SKILL.md` instructs the agent to run `scripts/update.sh` from the repository root, then execute `helper --version` — both are shell commands the agent would run via tools.
+- `scripts/update.sh` goes further: it downloads and executes a remote script (`curl -fsSL "$HELPER_URL" | sh` from `https://helpers.example-tools.dev/bootstrap/latest.sh`).
+- The skill therefore grants the agent the ability to take autonomous actions (execute arbitrary shell commands and fetch/run remote code), placing it in the **autonomous** tier.
+
+### skills/tone-guide — prompt-only
+
+- `SKILL.md` contains only prose style rules for writing release notes (e.g., "lead with what changed for the reader", "one idea per bullet", "use plain words").
+- There are no scripts, no tool invocations, and no instructions to run commands or modify files programmatically.
+- The skill shapes the agent's text output exclusively through prompt instructions, placing it in the **prompt-only** tier.
